## 🚀 How to Run Your App Properly

### Prerequisites

```bash
# Check Node.js version (requires 18+)
node --version

# Check npm
npm --version

# Ensure MongoDB is accessible
# Ensure Redis is running (optional but recommended)
```

### Step 1: Install Dependencies

```bash
cd /Users/arpitchoudhary/Downloads/Veefore_v3/Veefore-E

# Install root dependencies
npm install

# Install client dependencies
cd client && npm install && cd ..

# Install admin panel dependencies (if needed)
cd admin-panel && npm install && cd ..
```

### Step 2: Environment Configuration

Your [.env](file:///Users/arpitchoudhary/Downloads/Veefore_v3/Veefore-E/server/.env) file is already configured in [server/.env](file:///Users/arpitchoudhary/Downloads/Veefore_v3/Veefore-E/server/.env). Verify these critical keys:

```bash
# Check if all required keys are set
cat server/.env | grep -E "(MONGODB_URI|FIREBASE|OPENAI|INSTAGRAM)"
```

### Step 3: Start Development Server

```bash
# From the root directory (Veefore-E)
npm run dev
```

This will:
- Start the Express backend on port 5000
- Start the Vite dev server for the frontend
- Connect to MongoDB
- Initialize all services

### Step 4: Access the Application

```
Frontend: http://localhost:5000
API: http://localhost:5000/api
Health Check: http://localhost:5000/api/health
Admin Panel: http://localhost:5000/admin
```

### Alternative: Run Client and Server Separately

```bash
# Terminal 1 - Backend
npm run dev

# Terminal 2 - Frontend (if needed separately)
npm run client:dev
```

